id: pm-g8oh0f
title: Omit redundant read receipts when canonical output flags do not compact results
description: "Canonical output flags reportedly add a verbose read_output receipt even when every requested field and row fits, unlike equivalent legacy flags."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-18T03:55:18.223Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-18T09:45:09.865Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-18T09:45:09.254Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-18T09:45:09.254Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Return compact output for no-op canonical output controls while preserving explicit audit requests and all actionable omission, fallback, truncation and continuation evidence."
parent: pm-5t33or
severity: medium
repro_steps: "Compare a one-item read with default output and --output-limit 20: reporter measured 183 bytes / 6 lines versus 572 bytes / 25 lines. Compare list 3 with legacy versus canonical flags: 875 bytes / 33 lines versus 1409 bytes / 57 lines."
resolution: "Omitted redundant receipts for non-binding canonical amount, cost and encoding requests; retained explicit audit/include/session/continuation receipts and prepared validation diagnostic declarations before no-op checks."
expected_result: Canonical no-op reads preserve all useful rows and fields without redundant receipt overhead; explicit or structurally required evidence remains available.
actual_result: "8997 tests pass at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; one-row SDK JSON falls from 172 to 25 tokens; complete-list, nested diagnostics, real mutation encoding and packed-consumer acceptance pass."
affected_version: 2026.9.17
component: SDK read-output budgets
