comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T03:55:18.223Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: searched all statuses for the issue numbers and precise largest-prefix and receipt-overhead wording; inspected the canonical output-budget parent and closed read fallback lineage; inspected current open and in-progress inventories. No existing focused item owns this newly reported behavior. Keep this intake open and unclaimed until implementation starts."
  "2026-09-18T08:29:35.755Z","harness:codex","no-op output-limit, output-format and output-budget cases initially emitted redundant receipts; they now preserve the original result when it fits. Explicit include projections, session accounting, continuation and output-row-contract requests retain receipts. Mutation-format validation and real CLI lifecycle coverage are in the same delivery under pm-srns."
  "2026-09-18T08:30:57.655Z","harness:codex","Live repository inventory: all 2772 recorded items participate in one connected knowledge graph with 13837 directed edges, zero orphans, no execution/hierarchy cycles, and a 12-layer execution graph. Seven grandfathered hierarchy inconsistencies remain; zero active violations. GitHub open PRs, Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning alerts are empty at intake. Dependency inventory has no wanted-version updates; major-version migrations remain separate compatibility work. Current work adds implements edges to the canonical output-contract owner rather than artificial depth."
  "2026-09-18T08:51:14.791Z","harness:codex","Latest stable-build manual acceptance in a fresh temporary directory passed: 131 items through the public SDK, Node/Bun mutation lifecycle using canonical encoding, pre-mutation read-only flag refusal, no-op receipt elision, and opt-in audit receipts. Requests of 20/30/40/50/60/80/100/130 rows now retain 12 rows consistently at 1443-1444 rendered JSON tokens under a 1500 ceiling. Discovery schema no longer reserves serialized budget when hidden."
  "2026-09-18T08:54:31.599Z","harness:codex","The repository agent-task token gate caught an unintended 350-token contracts discovery receipt. Restricted the explicit-full certification exception to list reads, where complete-list SDK validation requires it. Added a full-contracts no-op regression; complete-list certification and unchanged task token baselines are required before closeout. No token or quality thresholds were loosened."
  "2026-09-18T09:16:19.078Z","harness:codex","Differential SDK measurement against the unchanged main implementation using the same one-row list payload and canonical outputLimit/outputFormat: rendered JSON falls from 172 tokens with the redundant receipt to 25 tokens without it. This isolates receipt overhead; it is not a whole-workspace benchmark. Full contracts snapshot and public SDK snapshot checks pass with zero classified API changes. Latest pm-changelog is 2026.9.18 and its repository has no open issues or PRs."
  "2026-09-18T09:18:06.928Z","harness:codex","The completed stable-source suite passed 8995 tests and found one regression: a no-op validate request skipped enrichment of nested diagnostic continuation paths. Moved structural continuation declaration before receipt-elision eligibility, preserving nested resume contracts without reintroducing the redundant receipt. The existing diagnostic continuation regression is the red-first guard. Coverage was not produced because that test failed; no 100-percent claim is made from the failed run."
  "2026-09-18T09:45:08.524Z","harness:codex","Final verification passed: all 8997 tests across 705 files; exact 100/100/100/100 coverage with no uncovered statements, branches, functions or lines. Explicit receipts, complete-list certificates, SDK/CLI transport parity and nested validate diagnostic declarations remain intact. The controlled one-row comparison falls from 172 to 25 JSON tokens; real temporary-workspace and packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx acceptance pass. No coverage threshold or ignore directive changed."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T09:32:58.703Z","harness:codex","Receipt elision is an optimization after structural contract preparation. Validation diagnostic declarations, complete-list certificates, session accounting and explicit audit requests must survive a no-op request. A cheaper payload is valid only when it preserves those consumer-visible obligations."
