body: "GitHub report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1267\n\nCanonical amount, cost, and encoding options no longer add read_output receipts when the existing result already fits and no transformation or audit receipt is needed. Explicit row-contract/audit requests, include projections, complete-list certificates, sessions, and continuations retain their evidence. Validation diagnostic row declarations are prepared before the no-op decision, preserving nested continuation support.\n\nThe same one-row SDK payload drops from 172 rendered JSON tokens to 25 with no row or field loss. This is an isolated receipt-overhead comparison, not a whole-workspace benchmark. Existing complete-list, transport, migration-hint, and validation continuation tests protect the retained contracts; real CLI/SDK acceptance covers the public behavior. See comments and linked test runs for current verification status."
